An abbreviation definition after a plus is skipped like a link definition

```
- +
*[A]: b
text

A
.
<ul>
  <li>text</li>
</ul>
<p><abbr title="b">A</abbr></p>
```

```
:: t
: +
*[A]: b
text

A
.
<dl>
  <dt>t</dt>
  <dd>text</dd>
</dl>
<p><abbr title="b">A</abbr></p>
```

```
> +
*[A]: b
text

A
.
<blockquote><p>text</p></blockquote>
<p><abbr title="b">A</abbr></p>
```

```
> - +
> *[A]: b
> text

A
.
<blockquote>
  <ul>
    <li>*[A]: b
text</li>
  </ul>
</blockquote>
<p>A</p>
```

```
- x
  - +
  *[A]: b
  text

A
.
<ul>
  <li>x
    <ul>
      <li>*[A]: b
text</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>
<p>A</p>
```

```
- +
 *[A]: b
text

A
.
<ul>
  <li>+</li>
</ul>
<p>text</p>
<p><abbr title="b">A</abbr></p>
```
